<section class="sec" id="case">
  <div class="case-head gut" data-reveal-group="up" data-reveal-stagger="160">
    <div>
      <span class="label mono"><i class="o"></i>Case study</span>
      <h2>There really is a faster way to scale <em>new heights</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="lead">OFAT, DoE and Trellis were benchmarked on the same virtual 12-factor CHO fed-batch process. Trellis reached effectively the full known optimum; DoE plateaued near 77%, OFAT near 50%.</p>
      <p class="lead">The difference is where the experiments go. OFAT searches locally, DoE spreads broadly and wastes runs far from the optimum, Trellis explores uncertain regions and concentrates where better performance is most likely.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="conv">
    <div class="conv-cv"><canvas id="convCv" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of percent of known optimum titre against experiments run. Trellis climbs fastest and reaches 99% of the known optimum; DoE reaches 77%; OFAT reaches 50%. Each line has a shaded uncertainty band."></canvas></div>
  </div>
  <p class="foot-note mono" data-reveal="fade">% of known optimum reached on a simulated 12-factor CHO fed-batch process.</p>
</section>
